{% if word_count %}You are playing a game in rounds. In each round you move a figure on a {{ grid_size }}x{{ grid_size }} grid of squares. Each square holds one English word, and the {{ grid_size * grid_size }} words on a grid are all different. The words are drawn every round from a vocabulary of {{ word_count }} words that neither you nor your partner is shown in full, and the grids change every round.

Your partner, another player, moves a second figure on a second grid of the same size. Your partner's grid is drawn separately from yours, so the same square on the two grids usually holds a different word. Every round, at least one word appears on both grids, and there can be more than one. You see which square your partner is on and every move your partner makes, and your partner sees the same of you. {% if partner_colours_visible %}Each of you sees the words of both grids.{% else %}Neither of you sees the words of the other's grid.{% endif %} You and your partner score a point together when you both finish on squares holding the same word. Coordinate with your partner. After each round, both grids are shown to both of you.
{% elif fills %}You are playing a game in rounds. In each round you move a figure on a {{ grid_size }}x{{ grid_size }} grid of squares. Each square holds one item: a shape, in a colour, with a fill, named fill first, then colour, then shape. The colours are: {{ colours | join(", ") }}. The shapes are: {{ shapes | join(", ") }}. The fills are: {{ fills | join(", ") }}. These lists are in orders drawn at random for you alone, and they stay the same in every round; your partner's instructions list the same colours, the same shapes and the same fills in orders drawn separately. An item can appear on several squares of a grid, or on none, and the grids change every round.

Your partner, another player, moves a second figure on a second grid of the same size. Your partner's grid is drawn separately from yours, so the same square on the two grids usually holds a different item. Every round, at least one item appears on both grids, and there can be more than one. You see which square your partner is on and every move your partner makes, and your partner sees the same of you. {% if partner_colours_visible %}Each of you sees the items of both grids.{% else %}Neither of you sees the items of the other's grid.{% endif %} You and your partner score a point together when you both finish on squares holding the same item: the same shape, in the same colour, with the same fill. Coordinate with your partner. After each round, both grids are shown to both of you.
{% elif shapes %}You are playing a game in rounds. In each round you move a figure on a {{ grid_size }}x{{ grid_size }} grid of squares. Each square holds one shape in one colour. The colours are: {{ colours | join(", ") }}. The shapes are: {{ shapes | join(", ") }}. These lists are in orders drawn at random for you alone, and they stay the same in every round; your partner's instructions list the same colours and the same shapes in orders drawn separately. A coloured shape can appear on several squares of a grid, or on none, and the grids change every round.

Your partner, another player, moves a second figure on a second grid of the same size. Your partner's grid is drawn separately from yours, so the same square on the two grids usually holds a different coloured shape. Every round, at least one coloured shape appears on both grids, and there can be more than one. You see which square your partner is on and every move your partner makes, and your partner sees the same of you. {% if partner_colours_visible %}Each of you sees the coloured shapes of both grids.{% else %}Neither of you sees the coloured shapes of the other's grid.{% endif %} You and your partner score a point together when you both finish on squares holding the same shape in the same colour. Coordinate with your partner. After each round, both grids are shown to both of you.
{% else %}You are playing a game in rounds. In each round you move a figure on a {{ grid_size }}x{{ grid_size }} grid of coloured squares. Each square is one of these colours: {{ colours | join(", ") }}. This list is in an order drawn at random for you alone, and it stays the same in every round; your partner's instructions list the same colours in an order drawn separately. A colour can appear on several squares of a grid, or on none, and the colours change every round.

Your partner, another player, moves a second figure on a second grid of the same shape. Your partner's grid is drawn separately from yours, so the same square on the two grids usually has a different colour. Every round, at least one colour appears on both grids, and there can be more than one. You see which square your partner is on and every move your partner makes, and your partner sees the same of you. {% if partner_colours_visible %}Each of you sees the colours of both grids.{% else %}Neither of you sees the colours of the other's grid.{% endif %} You and your partner score a point together when you both finish on squares of the same colour. Coordinate with your partner. After each round, both grids are shown to both of you.
{% endif %}
Score as many rounds as you can.

Each figure starts every round on a square chosen at random, separately for you and your partner; the round's briefing says where both start. Rows count down from the top and columns right from the left. You have {{ moves_per_round }} moves per round: up, down, left and right each spend one. One move call can make up to {{ max_moves_per_call }} of them in a row, and your partner sees each one. A move off the grid is refused and spends nothing. Call end_round when you are on your final square, which then cannot change. If the round ends before you call end_round, the square you stand on counts. A round ends once both figures have finished, or after {{ round_seconds }} seconds.
